  8. WHAT THIS REPORT EXERCISES, SCOPED ACCURATELY
  This class is one of the eleven API controller tests in this module. It covers TASK LOOKUP BY
  IDENTIFIER, a general task API read endpoint, and it is expressly NOT one of the six controller tests
  that form the API level surface of the workflow engine. Those six cover claim and unclaim, completion,
  completion with an outcome, business process creation, process instance deletion and workflow history.
  This report belongs to the other five, the general task API members, alongside ad hoc task creation,
  task removal, listing all tasks and task saving. That distinction is stated plainly because inflating a
  general read endpoint into engine surface evidence would misdescribe what this row proves, and the
  honest limits in section 10 depend on the distinction holding.
  The REST contracts these controllers expose, meaning paths, verbs, request and response shapes and
  authentication behaviour, are preserved with no controller signature, request mapping or serialised
  field change. Deliberately, none of that contract is transcribed into this report: no path, no verb, no
  request body and no response body appears below, even though the source of record contains all four. A
  report records WHICH test case existed, not what the endpoint looks like, and restating a preserved
  contract inside the evidence for it would add a second place for it to drift.
  This class extends EasyMockSupport, so this report is part of the before picture for the mocking
  library whose floor advance carries the widest POM footprint in the whole migration: the installed
  release AND the intermediate release fail identically on the target runtime with an inaccessible object
